While doing this project, I encountered a lot of problems and failures. Starting from a wrong Python interpreter in my VS Code. All projects were working before I closed my VS Code app, but when I opened it after several days, it was not working anymore. I tried installing and reinstalling the OpenCV module and Ultralytics (pip install opencv-python ultralytics), but it still doesn’t work. Then, after reading a lot of troubleshooting guides on the internet, I found out that I’m using a different Python interpreter between the terminal and editor environments. This solves my problem for several days. 

As I progressed in developing this project, I encountered an error called “UnboundLocalError” in my Motion Detection Section. This occurred when I was accessing the previous grayscale frame during the motion detection to calculate the motion score. I think the cause of this is the variable holding the previous frame before being initialized in the first loop iteration. What I did in my program to solve this is to use a try-except block. I made an exception for UnboundLocalError for the program to continue or pass or just print something for it to move on to the next line of code.

Another failure that I encountered is that I need to press ‘r’ (to restart the game), ‘s’ (to start the game), and ‘e’ (to exit) several times before it executes. I think the cause of this is debouncing, or the key pressed was missed due to the frame processing delays. What I did to solve this is to ensure that cv2.waitkey() was only called once per loop because the first time I used this code, I used it separately for the three conditions.

